# TypeScript & React Native (this repo)

Applies when working under `app/`, `components/`, `hooks/`, `store/`, `context/`, `services/` (or similar).

## Authority

- `.cursor/skills/react-native-coding-standards/SKILL.md` is the extended standard. Align naming, structure, and quality with it.

## Structure

- Routes/screens: `app/`. Reusable UI: `components/`. Hooks: `hooks/`. API/business logic: prefer `services/` or dedicated hooks — keep components thin.

## TypeScript

- New UI code: TypeScript only. Explicit `Props` types (or equivalent) for components; type async returns as `Promise<...>` where it matters. Avoid `any`; if unavoidable, `TODO` comment.

## Components

- Function components + hooks only. No side effects in render; `useEffect` / handlers for I/O and navigation.

## Async

- Handle loading, error, and empty states for user-visible data.
- Never fire-and-forget promises without handling errors.
- For **global blocking** UX, use `showLoader` / `hideLoader` (see `esports-project-conventions` rule).

## Styling

- Prefer `StyleSheet.create` or shared style patterns in the file. Use theme tokens (`colors`, spacing) — avoid magic color hex in new code unless matching an existing pattern.

## Naming

- Components / files: `PascalCase`. Hooks: `useThing.ts`, `useThing`. Variables/functions: `camelCase`.
